[{"role": "assistant", "content": "```php
function extractFunctionCalls($phpCode) {
    $pattern = '/(?<!\/\*.*)(?<!\/\/.*)\b\w+\s*\([^)]*\);/';
    preg_match_all($pattern, $phpCode, $matches);
    return $matches[0];
}
```

The `extractFunctionCalls` function uses a regular expression pattern to match function calls in the given PHP code. The pattern `/(?<!\/\*.*)(?<!\/\/.*)\b\w+\s*\([^)]*\);/` ensures that it ignores function calls within comments by using negative lookbehind assertions `(?<!\/\*.*)(?<!\/\/.*)` to exclude matches that occur within `/* */` or `//` comments. The function then uses `preg_match_all` to find all matches of the pattern in the input `phpCode` and returns the list of function calls found."}]

