[{"role": "assistant", "content": "```php
namespace app\controllers;

use Yii;
use yii\web\Controller;

class FormatterController extends Controller
{
    public function formatString($input)
    {
        // Check if the input contains only lowercase letters
        if (ctype_lower($input)) {
            return strtoupper($input); // Convert to uppercase
        }
        // Check if the input contains only uppercase letters
        elseif (ctype_upper($input)) {
            return strtolower($input); // Convert to lowercase
        }
        else {
            $formattedString = '';
            $isUpper = true; // Start with uppercase
            for ($i = 0; $i < strlen($input); $i++) {
                if (ctype_alpha($input[$i])) {
                    if ($isUpper) {
                        $formattedString .= strtoupper($input[$i]);
                    } else {
                        $formattedString .= strtolower($input[$i]);
                    }
                    $isUpper = !$isUpper; // Toggle case for next character
                } else {
                    $formattedString .= $input[$i]; // Keep non-alphabetic characters unchanged
                }
            }
            return $formattedString;
        }
    }
}
```

The `formatString` method first checks if the input contains only lowercase or uppercase letters using `ctype_lower` and `ctype_upper` functions. If so, it converts the input to the opposite case using `strtolower` or `strtoupper` functions. If the input contains a mix of uppercase and lowercase letters, it iterates through each character, converting them to alternating case and preserving non-alphabetic characters."}]

