[{"role": "assistant", "content": "```php
function calculateDistance($latitudes, $longitudes) {
    $distance = 0;
    $radius = 6371; // Earth's radius in kilometers

    // Calculate distance for individual points
    if (count($latitudes) == 1) {
        return $distance; // No movement, distance is 0
    }

    // Calculate distance for line string
    for ($i = 1; $i < count($latitudes); $i++) {
        $lat1 = deg2rad($latitudes[$i - 1]);
        $lon1 = deg2rad($longitudes[$i - 1]);
        $lat2 = deg2rad($latitudes[$i]);
        $lon2 = deg2rad($longitudes[$i]);

        $dlat = $lat2 - $lat1;
        $dlon = $lon2 - $lon1;

        $a = sin($dlat / 2) * sin($dlat / 2) + cos($lat1) * cos($lat2) * sin($dlon / 2) * sin($dlon / 2);
        $c = 2 * atan2(sqrt($a), sqrt(1 - $a));
        $distance += $radius * $c;
    }

    return $distance;
}
```

This solution provides a function `calculateDistance` that accurately calculates the total distance traveled based on the input coordinates, considering both individual points and line strings. The Haversine formula is used to account for the Earth's curvature, ensuring accurate distance calculations."}]

