The time complexity of this approach is O(n), where n is the number of characters in the string, because we're looping through the string once. The space complexity is also O(n), considering that we're building a new output string.

Here is a PHP code snippet:

```php
function removeSpecialCharacters($str) {
    $result = "";

    for($i = 0; $i < strlen($str); $i++) {
        $ascii = ord($str[$i]);

        // Consider only alphanumeric (A-Z, a-z, 0-9) and space characters
        if(($ascii >= 48 && $ascii <= 57) || // 0-9
           ($ascii >= 65 && $ascii <= 90) || // A-Z
           ($ascii >= 97 && $ascii <= 122) || // a-z
           $ascii == 32) { // space
            $result .= $str[$i];
        }
    }

    return $result;
}

$str = "Hello, World! #123";
echo removeSpecialCharacters($str); // Output: "Hello World 123"
```
This script defines the function removeSpecialCharacters(), which scans through the string character by character. If a character is alphanumeric or a space, it is appended to the resultant string; if not, it is skipped. At the end of the function, the resultant string, without any special characters, is returned."}]

