[{"role": "assistant", "content": "A factorial of a number n (represented as n!) is the product of all positive integers less than or equal to n. To compute it, you may use the iterative method or recursive method. Here's how you can do it in PHP.

Iterative version:

```php
function factorial($n) {
    $result = 1;
    for ($i = 1; $i <= $n; $i++) {
        $result *= $i;
    }
    return $result;
}
```

Recursive version:

```php
function factorial($n) {
    if ($n == 0) {
        return 1;
    } else {
        return $n * factorial($n - 1);
    }
}
```

Each function will take a numerical input (n) and calculate the factorial by multiplying the numbers from 1 to n. 

Please note that as the number n gets larger, the result can easily exceed the maximum integer values that can be held in PHP variables. Thus, PHP may return incorrect results for large input numbers. It's also worth noticing that the recursive function can cause a stack overflow if the input number is large enough, due to the large amount of recursive calls."}]

